  "description": "Business Payment Controls create-project flow. Authored 2026-05-29 from a recorder session (project 'testbizpaycontrols2'). The recorder captured all selectors but dropped the click_proceed steps because BPC's Proceed button wraps its label in a <span>, and the recorder's _is_proceed() detector keys off the inner element's data-testid (which is empty on the <span>). The proceed clicks have been re-inserted manually below; they fire on the outer button[data-testid='proceed-btn'] which the runner already targets via click_proceed. BPC's wizard has 4 steps (not 3 like most APIs): (1) Project details, (2) Service details / regtoken, (3) Project credentials (OAuth1 signing key), (4) Additional credentials (Mastercard encryption key). Steps 3 and 4 each need their own Proceed click; the Step-4 encryption inputs remain hidden in the DOM until Step-3 Proceed advances the wizard.",
  "recorded_at": "2026-05-29T14:19:24Z",
  "start_url": "https://developer.mastercard.com/create-project?services=business-payment-controls",
  "final_url_pattern": "/project-details/",
  "variables": [
    "project_name",
    "alias",
    "key_password",
    "contact_email",
    "registration_token"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "registration_token": "123456789"
  },
  "steps": [
    { "action": "wait_for", "selector": "input[data-testid='project-name']" },
    { "action": "fill", "selector": "input[data-testid='project-name']", "value": "{{project_name}}", "delay_ms": 60 },
    { "action": "sleep", "ms": 500 },
    { "action": "screenshot", "name": "bpc_step1_project_name_filled" },
